2 diabetes mellitus for the past few years. She
has presented to your clinic in distress
because she has started bumping into
objects since this morning. She also says that
she has been seeing floaters and flies in front
of her eyes for the past three days. Eye
examination reveals vision loss and
decreased red reflex of the right eye. The
right retina cannot be visualised. The left
eye''s vision iS preserved; however, retinal
changes are consistent with pre-proliferative
diabetic retinopathy. Which one of the
