with an 8-month right ankle swelling and pain
history. The patient relates that the ankle is stiff
in the morning, taking over one hour of walking
and physical activity to ease up. No other joint is
involved. On examination, she has a
temperature of 36.9°C with other vital signs
within normal limits. The right ankle joint is
swollen, has a restricted range of motion, and is
slightly tender. An X-ray of the right ankle and
foot shows periarticular osteopenia and
narrowed joint space of the right ankle. Which of
the following could be this presentation''s most
likely underlying cause?','{"A":"Septic arthritis.","B":"Osteomyelitis.","C":"Systemic lupus erythematosus\n(SLE).","D":"Rheumatoid arthritis (RA).","E":"Osteoarthritis (OA)."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Orthopaedic  (1).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-a452780dee0e","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"6bbd9daec639a3db8d84","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Orthopaedic  (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Orthopaedic  (1).pdf","source_page":27,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"five_block_inferred","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','low','{"record_id":"6bbd9daec639a3db8d84","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Orthopaedic  (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Orthopaedic  (1).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":27,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Orthopaedics/Rheumatology","stem":"A 47-year-old woman presents to your clinic\nwith an 8-month right ankle swelling and pain\nhistory. The patient relates that the ankle is stiff\nin the morning, taking over one hour of walking\nand physical activity to ease up. No other joint is\ninvolved. On examination, she has a\ntemperature of 36.9°C with other vital signs\nwithin normal limits. The right ankle joint is\nswollen, has a restricted range of motion, and is\nslightly tender. An X-ray of the right ankle and\nfoot shows periarticular osteopenia and\nnarrowed joint space of the right ankle. Which of\nthe following could be this presentation''s most\nlikely underlying cause?","options":{"A":"Septic arthritis.","B":"Osteomyelitis.","C":"Systemic lupus erythematosus\n(SLE).","D":"Rheumatoid arthritis (RA).","E":"Osteoarthritis (OA)."},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import"