department with an acutely painful left index
finger, shown in the following photograph. On
examination, she is afebrile, and the right
finger''s distal interphalangeal (DIP) joint is red,
warm, and extremely tender to touch with
decreased motion due to pain. She has had four
episodes of such incidents in the past two years
in the same finger, diagnosed as recurrent
gouty arthritis. She is currently on a prophylactic
dose of colchicine and allopurinol 100 mg daily.
she is also a known case of long-standing
hypertension, controlled on hydrochlorothiazide
and metoprolol, and also a known case of
hypertensive nephropathy. Which one of the
following would you consider for her as the first-
line treatment option at this stage?','{"A":"Cessation of allopurinol.","B":"Indomethacin.","C":"Celecoxib.","D":"Prednisolone for 10 days.","E":"Increasing the dose of allopurinol to\n150 mg daily."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Orthopaedic  (1).pdf","supporting_pages":[145,147],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-d5addef131ec","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"47ea80b1b0aebf206a88","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Orthopaedic  (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Orthopaedic  (1).pdf","source_page":145,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.9.2-manual-context-utility-complete-2026-09-23","parser_mode":"v29_cross_page_backward_context","text_method":"v291_existing_context+v29_ocr_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,'text',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"47ea80b1b0aebf206a88","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Orthopaedic  (1).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Orthopaedic  (1).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":145,"supporting_pages":[145,147],"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Orthopaedics/Rheumatology","stem":"Laura, 56 years old, presents to the emergency\ndepartment with an acutely painful left index\nfinger, shown in the following photograph. On\nexamination, she is afebrile, and the right\nfinger''s distal interphalangeal (DIP) joint is red,\nwarm, and extremely tender to touch with\ndecreased motion due to pain. She has had four\nepisodes of such incidents in the past two years\nin the same finger, diagnosed as recurrent\ngouty arthritis. She is currently on a prophylactic\ndose of colchicine and allopurinol 100 mg daily.\nshe is also a known case of long-standing\nhypertension, controlled on hydrochlorothiazide\nand metoprolol, and also a known case of\nhypertensive nephropathy. Which one of the\nfollowing would you consider for her as the first-\nline treatment option at thi