sensation of foreign body in her eyes, eye
itching, and dry mouth for the past 6 months.
She also reveals that she has recently
developed a dry cough and pain in the hand
joints. On examination, there is mild bilateral
swelling of the parotid glands. The
metacarpophalangeal (MCP) and proximal
interphalangeal (PIP) are tender to touch, but
not warm or swollen. She denies any morning
Stiffness. Serologic tests are significant for a
positive ANA and RF. ESR and CRP are
elevated. Urinalysis is normal. Which one of the
