with the complaint of a painful right elbow. The
pain is felt laterally radiating to the back of the
forearm, aggravates with activity, and relieves
with rest. He is a carpenter and makes cabinets.
His job includes lots of sawing, drilling, and
using screwdrivers. On examination, you notice
a tender point 1-2 cm distal to the right lateral
epicondyle. Extension of the wrist with the
elbow in full extension brings up the pain. Which
one of the following is the most appropriate next
step in management?','{"A":"Physiotherapy.","B":"Advising himr to quit his job.","C":"GC Intralesional corticosteroids.","D":"Surgery.","E":"Band support below the elbow."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Orthopaedic  (2).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-a76d7218ee97","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"6264a1ef0c9654dd33b3","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Orthopaedic  (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Orthopaedic  (2).pdf","source_page":67,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"five_block_inferred","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"6264a1ef0c9654dd33b3","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Orthopaedic  (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Orthopaedic  (2).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":67,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Orthopaedics/Rheumatology","stem":"A 45-year-old man presents to your GP clinic\nwith the complaint of a painful right elbow. The\npain is felt laterally radiating to the back of the\nforearm, aggravates with activity, and relieves\nwith rest. He is a carpenter and makes cabinets.\nHis job includes lots of sawing, drilling, and\nusing screwdrivers. On examination, you notice\na tender point 1-2 cm distal to the right lateral\nepicondyle. Extension of the wrist with the\nelbow in full extension brings up the pain. Which\none of the following is the most appropriate next\nstep in management?","options":{"A":"Physiotherapy.","B":"Advising himr to quit his job.","C":"GC Intralesional corticosteroids.","D":"Surgery.","E":"Band support below the elbow."},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence