with progressive low back pain that is shooting
and radiates to her left buttock. She denies any
preceding trauma or sprain. Her medical history
is significant for breast cancer treated with
mastectomy, chemotherapy, and radiotherapy
six years ago and osteoarthritis of the
lumbosacral spine. On examination, there is
tenderness over the L4/L5 area, and a
positive straight leg raise (SLR) test on the left
side. Which of the following features in the
clinical assessment is an indication for further
assessments of this patient?','{"A":"Absence of a preceding trauma or\nsprain.","B":"Osteoarthritis of the lumbosacral\nspine.","C":"Positive SLR test.","D":"The radicular nature of her pain.","E":"Past history of breast cancer."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Orthopaedic  (2).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-6b7e0cf5d965","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"0dac66e53d656dc61f63","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Orthopaedic  (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Orthopaedic  (2).pdf","source_page":86,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"five_block_inferred","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"0dac66e53d656dc61f63","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 Orthopaedic  (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 Orthopaedic  (2).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":86,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Orthopaedics/Rheumatology","stem":"A 49-year-old woman presents to your GP clinic\nwith progressive low back pain that is shooting\nand radiates to her left buttock. She denies any\npreceding trauma or sprain. Her medical history\nis significant for breast cancer treated with\nmastectomy, chemotherapy, and radiotherapy\nsix years ago and osteoarthritis of the\nlumbosacral spine. On examination, there is\ntenderness over the L4/L5 area, and a\npositive straight leg raise (SLR) test on the left\nside. Which of the following features in the\nclinical assessment is an indication for further\nassessments of this patient?","options":{"A":"Absence of a preceding trauma or\nsprain.","B":"Osteoarthritis of the lumbosacral\nspine.","C":"Positive SLR test.","D":"The radicular nature of her pain.","E":"Past history of breast cancer."},"source_answer":null,"source_explanat